  "question": {
    "text": "In Young's double slit experiment the two slits are d distance apart. Interference pattern is observed on a screen at a distance D from the slits. A dark fringe is observed on the screen directly opposite to one of the slits. The wavelength of light is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wlfOv",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{D}^2}{2 \\mathrm{~d}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "I6YEv",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}^2}{2 \\mathrm{D}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BDVBF",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{D}^2}{\\mathrm{~d}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BdUPx",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}^2}{\\mathrm{D}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/YELJhfyCXGImSRqAppODWI6pyWPkKEZyjYNUm5nuSQc.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\\(\\mathrm{n}^{\\text {th }}\\) Dark fringe\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& (2 n-1) \\frac{D \\lambda}{2 d}=\\frac{d}{2} \\\\\n& \\lambda=\\frac{d^2}{(2 n-1) D}=\\frac{d^2}{D} \\quad[\\text { for } n=1]\n\\end{aligned}\\)",
